Import a confirmed catalog GLB from `scene_builder_3d_search_assets` into the selected project
as a collaborative scene entity. Supply the catalog's asset ID, not a URL. The tool runtime
resolves and uploads the bytes, reads the project guards, submits the import, and waits for
it to appear in the settled scene. Do not import while another mutation is active. After
import, inspect dimensions, placement, orientation, contact, and materials with
`scene_builder_3d_query_python` before further edits. Do not repeat the whole import to poll:
it can create a duplicate. If an import fails, report the error; never fall back to Python
network calls or base64-encoded model bytes. Copy catalogSearch from the search result's importArguments. If settled is false, poll scene_builder_3d_get_project until appliedSceneSequence reaches targetSceneSequence. If submissionUnknown is true, inspect the returned entityId before deciding to retry. This version accepts catalog assets only.

Finish each completed scene creation, edit, or import task by calling `scene_builder_3d_show_scene` once as the final scene inspection/edit call of that review phase, after mutations have settled and verification is complete. Pass the same `projectId` and the exact committed `revision` of the final result: `revisionAfter` from the final successful mutation, or the settled `project.revision` after an import. Do not guess the revision. Show an unchanged revision only once. Authorized generation and status calls may follow; later feedback or a verified mismatch can reopen scene editing. Verify and show the corrected revision at its next review boundary. This shows the result to the user; a text summary or download link alone does not finish scene delivery.

```ts
mcp__Higgsfield__scene_builder_3d_import_asset(args: {
// Confirmed catalog ID from scene_builder_3d_search_assets. Attachment IDs are not supported by this tool.
assetId: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 128
// Copy catalogSearch from the search result's importArguments so the catalog ID can be resolved in the same result set.
catalogSearch?: string, // default: "", maxLength: 128
name?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 128
// Stable ID for this logical operation. Reuse only for an identical request, including code and guards.
operationId: string, // pattern: /^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]{0,127}$/
// Project ID from scene_builder_3d_list_projects, scene_builder_3d_create_project, or the user's explicit selection. Required on every project-scoped tool.
projectId: string, // pattern: /^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$/, format: "uuid"
// Editor/glTF coordinates: metres, Y up, XYZW quaternion. Blender bpy coordinates are Z up; account for that when comparing transforms.
transform?: {
// default: [0, 0, 0], minItems: 3, maxItems: 3
position?: [
item0: number, // minimum: -1000000.0, maximum: 1000000.0
item1: number, // minimum: -1000000.0, maximum: 1000000.0
item2: number, // minimum: -1000000.0, maximum: 1000000.0
],
rotation?: [item0: number, item1: number, item2: number, item3: number], // default: [0, 0, 0, 1], minItems: 4, maxItems: 4
// default: [1, 1, 1], minItems: 3, maxItems: 3
scale?: [
item0: number, // minimum: 1e-06, maximum: 1000000.0
item1: number, // minimum: 1e-06, maximum: 1000000.0
item2: number, // minimum: 1e-06, maximum: 1000000.0
],
},
// Seconds to wait, capped at 8; poll scene_builder_3d_get_operation if still active.
waitSeconds?: integer, // default: 8, minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
}): Promise<{
appliedSceneSequence?: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
assetId: string,
entityId: string,
error?: { code: string, message: string, retryAdvice?: string, retryable: boolean },
name: string,
nextAction?: string,
nextTool?: "scene_builder_3d_get_project",
ok: boolean,
operationId: string,
projectId: string,
// Open this project in 3D Jutsu.
projectUrl: string, // format: "uri"
revision?: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
sceneSequence?: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
// Whether the accepted import has reached the committed scene.
settled?: boolean,
source: "catalog",
// Inspect entityId before retrying: the import may already have been accepted.
submissionUnknown?: boolean,
// Poll until appliedSceneSequence reaches this value.
targetSceneSequence?: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
}>;
```

Search the curated GLB model catalog available to 3D Jutsu. This read is authorized
against `projectId`; the catalog itself is shared. Pass a returned `assetId` to
`scene_builder_3d_import_asset` for the same selected project. Search results are available
models, not objects already present in the scene. Inspect existing scene objects with
`scene_builder_3d_query_python` before deciding what to add. Never invent an asset ID or turn
a catalog URL into Python download code. Copy the returned importArguments, including catalogSearch, into scene_builder_3d_import_asset.

```ts
mcp__Higgsfield__scene_builder_3d_search_assets(args: {
limit?: integer, // default: 100, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
// Project ID from scene_builder_3d_list_projects, scene_builder_3d_create_project, or the user's explicit selection. Required on every project-scoped tool.
projectId: string, // pattern: /^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$/, format: "uuid"
search?: string, // default: "", maxLength: 128
}): Promise<{
assets: { assetId: string, importArguments: { assetId: string, catalogSearch?: string, projectId: string }, name: string, tags: string[] }[],
ok: true,
// Open this project in 3D Jutsu.
projectUrl: string, // format: "uri"
total: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
}>;
```

Show an interactive 3D scene preview of an existing 3D Jutsu project. Choose projectId with scene_builder_3d_list_projects, scene_builder_3d_create_project, or the user's explicit selection. Pass revisionAfter from a successful edit to show that exact result, or omit revision for the latest committed GLB. Wait for edits to settle with scene_builder_3d_get_operation before showing their result. This reads an existing export; it never starts Blender, edits the scene, or includes uncommitted collaborative changes. Call this when the user asks to see the scene. For a completed scene creation, edit, or import task, call it once at the scene review boundary after settlement and verification. Do not repeat an unchanged revision. Authorized generation/status calls may follow; feedback or a verified mismatch can reopen editing and lead to a newly verified revision. The widget is for the user to inspect; it does not give the agent visual evidence. Use scene_builder_3d_query_python and scene_builder_3d_get_artifact for the agent's visual verification. If the client cannot display widgets, provide the returned projectUrl.

```ts
mcp__Higgsfield__scene_builder_3d_show_scene(args: {
// Project ID from scene_builder_3d_list_projects, scene_builder_3d_create_project, or the user's explicit selection. Required on every project-scoped tool.
projectId: string, // pattern: /^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$/, format: "uuid"
// Committed revision to preview. Omit for the latest committed revision; use revisionAfter to show the exact result of an edit.
revision?: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
}): Promise<{
artifact: {
etag: string,
height?:
 | integer // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
 | null
,
id?: string,
mediaType?: "image/png" | "image/jpeg" | "video/mp4",
name?: string,
operationId?: string,
projectId: string,
revision: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
size: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
type?: "glb" | "blend",
width?:
 | integer // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
 | null
,
},
download: {
expiresAt: string,
// Additional JSON Schema constraints: propertyNames={"type": "string"}
headers: { [key: string]: string },
method: "GET" | "PUT",
url: string, // format: "uri"
},
kind: "scene_builder_3d_scene",
ok: true,
projectId: string,
// Open this project in 3D Jutsu.
projectUrl: string, // format: "uri"
revision: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
}>;
```

Search the Epidemic Sound catalog by a natural-language sound description. Returns full titles, durations and opaque IDs, not audio URLs. Keep the same query and pass next_offset as offset for more results; null ends pagination. Use preview_sound_effect to listen, then download_sound_effect only for sounds selected for use in content. Catalog IDs are not FNF media IDs.

```ts
mcp__Higgsfield__search_sound_effects(args: {
limit?: integer, // default: 20, minimum: 1, maximum: 60
offset?: integer, // default: 0, minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
// Describe the sound you need in natural language.
query: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 500
}): Promise<{
error?: string,
// maxItems: 60
items?: Array<
{
duration_seconds: number, // minimum: 0.0
id: string, // pattern: /^epidemic_sound:[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/
provider: "epidemic_sound",
title: string,
}
>,
limit?: integer, // minimum: 1, maximum: 60
next_offset?:
 | integer // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
 | null
,
offset?: integer, // minimum: 0, maximum: 9007199254740991
}>;
```

Submit user-approved product feedback to Higgsfield through PostHog. Send feedback with send_feedback only after the user approves the exact report and optional job reference. A complaint alone is not consent. After addressing a meaningful failure, quality complaint or missing capability, offer once if useful; never interrupt successful work or repeat a declined offer. Exclude credentials, private prompts, media and full chat transcripts. Feedback is not support, a refund or a generation retry. If submission fails, report that briefly and continue the original task without automatic retries. Returns submitted only after the network submission succeeds; it does not promise a support reply. Identical reports are deduplicated for ten minutes.

```ts
mcp__Higgsfield__send_feedback(args: {
category?: "tool_error" | "generation_quality" | "missing_capability" | "confusing_output" | "documentation" | "other", // default: "other"
// Optional related generation job ID accessible to the authenticated user. Never invent an ID.
job_id?: string, // pattern: /^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$/, format: "uuid"
// The exact feedback text approved by the user, at most 2000 Unicode characters. Exclude credentials, private prompts, media URLs and chat transcripts.
message: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 2000
// low: minor friction; medium: workaround available; high: blocked
severity?: "low" | "medium" | "high", // default: "medium"
// Exact relevant Higgsfield tool name; omit if unrelated to a tool.
tool_name?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 100
}): Promise<{
feedback_id: string, // pattern: /^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$/, format: "uuid"
status: "submitted",
}>;
```

Extract full-length FLAC stems from up to 60 minutes of audio or video in the user's Higgsfield sandbox. Use for isolating vocals, removing vocals, or separating instruments, not for speech generation. Returns a background status file; use sandbox_exec to read it until completed or failed. Completed status lists stem paths. Do not resubmit to poll. To cancel, create the returned cancel_path in the sandbox.

```ts
mcp__Higgsfield__separate_stems(args: {
// two (default): vocals and no_vocals. four: vocals, drums, bass and other.
mode?: "two" | "four",
// New sandbox output directory. Defaults to a unique directory under stems/. Existing directories are never overwritten.
out_dir?: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 1024
// Existing audio or video file under /home/user in the caller's Higgsfield sandbox (not a URL, media ID or local attachment).
path: string, // minLength: 1, maxLength: 1024
}): Promise<{ cancel_path: string, expires_at: string, status: "running", status_path: string }>;
```

Use when the user asks to share a project with, invite, or give access to specific people, including creating a shared project (create_project first). Invites them by email with one role (view, collaborate or admin); default to view unless the user says otherwise. Same as inviting from the web Share dialog: invitees receive access to the project's content. Before calling, show the user exactly who gets which access and obtain explicit approval in this conversation; never infer emails. Requires confirm_share=true. Only owners and admins can invite; FNF enforces this. Do not retry an uncertain outcome; read get_project_sharing first.

```ts
mcp__Higgsfield__share_project(args: {
confirm_share: true,
// minItems: 1, maxItems: 10
emails: Array<
string // maxLength: 254, pattern: /^(?!\.)(?!.*\.\.)([A-Za-z0-9_'+\-\.]*)[A-Za-z0-9_+-]@([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9\-]*\.)+[A-Za-z]{2,}$/, format: "email"
>,
project_id: string, // pattern: /^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$/, format: "uuid"
// view: see the project; collaborate: generate and organize content; admin: also manage members and settings.
role: "view" | "collaborate" | "admin",
// Workspace context used for this request. This never changes the account's selected workspace.
workspace_id: string, // pattern: /^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$/, format: "uuid"
}): Promise<{
error?: string,
// Additional JSON Schema constraints: propertyNames={"type": "string"}
project?: { [key: string]: any },
[key: string]: any,
}>;
```

Display the final completed Katana video in its result widget with preview and download. Retained for backward compatibility; prefer show_result with action for new calls. Call after verifying the final export. Pass exactly one of media_id (a confirmed owned video UUID) or url (a public HTTPS video URL, up to 50 MB). URL input imports and confirms the video in your media library before displaying it. Prefer media_id for an already uploaded video to avoid duplicate uploads. Never pass a job ID, local path or unfinished render.

```ts
mcp__Higgsfield__show_katana_result(args: {
// Confirmed owned video UUID; omit when using url.
media_id?: string, // pattern: /^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$/, format: "uuid"
// Public HTTPS video URL, up to 50 MB; omit when using media_id.
url?: string, // format: "uri"
}): Promise<{
media_id: string, // pattern: /^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$/, format: "uuid"
mode: "result",
thumbnail_url?: string, // format: "uri"
video_url: string, // format: "uri"
}>;
```

