Show the user's latest uploaded media files of one type in the widget. Returns media IDs, URLs, and creation timestamps. Call once with the single type the user asked for (default image); do not enumerate other types unless requested. The widget handles pagination. Do not call show_medias again merely because next_cursor is present; use cursor only when the user explicitly asks for more items. Pass media IDs as value in the medias array of generation tools.

```ts
mcp__Higgsfield__show_medias(args: {
// Use a previous next_cursor only when the user explicitly asks for more items; otherwise omit.
cursor?: number,
// Number of results per page
size?: integer, // default: 24, minimum: 1, maximum: 100
// Media type to list. Defaults to image.
type?: "image" | "video" | "audio", // default: "image"
}): Promise<{
error?: string,
// Array of uploaded media files. Absent on error.
items?: { created_at: number, id: string, type: "image" | "video" | "audio", url: string }[],
// The media type this listing is for (echoes the request's type).
media_type?: "image" | "video" | "audio",
// Opaque cursor for widget pagination. Do not automatically call show_medias again when present.
next_cursor?: number | null,
}>;
```

Show the user the gallery of their reusable characters, environments and props. Omit element_id for a paginated gallery; supply element_id for one element with all its media. Call this to display Elements; to search or read them as data use elements_search and elements_get, and to create one use elements_create. USAGE IN GENERATION:
Embed `<<<element_id>>>` inside `params.prompt` of `generate_image` / `generate_video`. Backend auto-injects the image and rewrites to `@element_name`. Multiple placeholders per prompt OK.
Example: `"Cinematic portrait of <<<UUID>>> on a rooftop"`, `"<<<A>>> handing coffee to <<<B>>> in a Paris cafe"`.

SUPPORTED MODELS (`params.model` = machine name, friendly in parens):
- Image: `gpt_image_2_6` (GPT Image 2.6 Sunburst), `gpt_image_2_6_flare` (GPT Image 2.6 Flare), `nano_banana_pro` (Nano Banana Pro), `nano_banana_2` (Nano Banana 2), `gpt_image_2` (GPT Image 2), `seedream_v4_5` (Seedream 4.5), `seedream_v5_lite` (Seedream 5.0 lite), `cinematic_studio_2_5` (Cinema Studio Image 2.5).
- Video: `cinematic_studio_video_v2` (Cinema Studio Video 2), `cinematic_studio_3_0` (Cinema Studio Video 3.0), `seedance_2_0` (Seedance 2.0), `kling3_0` (Kling 3.0 — REQUIRES a `start_image` in `params.medias`; element placeholder alone won't trigger reference usage).
Map friendly names to model ids. Verify reference-element support before choosing other models. GPT Image 2.6 supports element references for raster and GIF output; SVG accepts no elements or image references.

USER-FACING STYLE: prefer friendly model names and element names for readability.

GUARDS:
- `@name` form does NOT work in tool calls — only `<<<UUID>>>` in `params.prompt`.
- Do NOT put element ids in `params.medias` / `params.input_images` — placeholder handles injection.
