Have RunComfy set up a ComfyUI workflow: a machine installs its custom nodes and models and saves it as a new version in My Workflows. This costs money.

    Call it first without `confirmed_price_usd`. That only returns the quote: the price ($0.20 for the
    account's first setup, $2.99 after that), the balance, and whether a pay-as-you-go account has
    room for another workflow. Tell the user the price, and that setup usually takes 30-60 minutes,
    or 2-3 hours when the workflow needs a different machine type. Only after they agree, call again
    with `confirmed_price_usd` set to the quoted price. Call it once per confirmation; if a call ends
    without an answer, check `list_workflow_setups` before trying again.

    After submitting, do not poll: check `get_workflow_setup_status` when it says to. RunComfy also
    emails the user when the setup finishes. When it is ready, `create_deployment` with its
    `workflow_id` and `workflow_version` publishes it as a Serverless API.


