Creates a new draft campaign. Audiences take real list or segment IDs from get_lists or get_segments, never placeholders; look one up first, even for a test campaign. A campaign holds default send settings (timezone, send strategy, exit condition) and one or more audiences; each message belongs to one audience and sends on one channel, and each message holds its content in one or more variations (more than one makes an A/B test). At least one audience is required. Create the structure inline (audiences with a temporary_id, and messages that reference one through audience_temporary_id, each with its variations; no variation is created for a message that omits them), or create a partial campaign and add the rest with create_campaign_audience, create_campaign_message, and create_campaign_variation. For email content, create a template with create_email_template, then set it as the variation's template_id or assign it with assign_template_to_campaign_message. Schedule each message with schedule_campaign_message, or send each message with send_campaign. You can view and edit a campaign in the Klaviyo UI at https://www.klaviyo.com/campaign/{CAMPAIGN_ID}/wizard

