Create a new drag-and-drop (DND, ``editor_type='SYSTEM_DRAGGABLE'``) email template, or update an existing one by setting ``body.data.id`` to its template ID. Unlike HTML templates created with create_email_template, DND templates use a structured definition describing sections, rows, columns, and blocks (text, image, button, etc.) — there is no raw HTML body. You can view and edit the template in the Klaviyo UI at https://www.klaviyo.com/email-template-editor/{TEMPLATE_ID}.

To create, omit ``body.data.id`` and send ``name``, ``editor_type`` and the full ``definition``. A static image block with a ``src`` must also have an ``asset_id`` (upload the image first with upload_image_from_url); leave static image blocks out when there is no uploaded image. Dynamic image blocks (``dynamic`` true) take a ``src`` and need no ``asset_id``.

To update, send any combination of name, definition, or text. The definition fully replaces the existing one — partial updates to individual sections/blocks are not supported. First retrieve the template with get_email_template, modify the definition, then pass the full definition here. If a template already contains universal blocks or sections, its definition cannot be updated, but its name and text can still change. You can also update the template of a flow email or a campaign message (get its template ID from get_flow_message or get_campaign_message). A campaign's template can be updated only while the campaign is a draft. A flow email in transactional review, and an A/B test variation of a transactional flow email, return a 409. Tell the user the reason and do not retry. If a flow email is transactional (get_flow_action shows definition.data.message.transactional as true), an update turns it into a marketing email that needs a new transactional review. Tell the user and get confirmation before you update it. Updating a flow email's template also requires the flows:write scope, and a campaign's template requires campaigns:write. A 403 that names a missing scope means the user must reconnect and grant it.

