Create a segment from a definition of condition groups, or update an existing segment by setting ``body.data.id`` to its segment ID. Condition groups are combined with AND, and conditions inside one group are combined with OR: a profile is in the segment only if it matches at least one condition in every group. When several things must all be true (for example, placed an order AND has no refunds AND has no cancellations), put each condition in its own condition group. Put conditions in the same group only when matching any one of them is enough.

To create, omit ``body.data.id`` and send ``name`` and ``definition``. Before calling this tool, restate the segment logic to the user in plain language using AND and OR explicitly, and confirm it matches what they intended.

To update, send any of name, starred status, active status, or definition. A definition sent on update replaces the existing definition entirely; omit definition to keep the current one. Before changing a definition, call get_segment to read the current one, tell the user in plain language what the segment matches now and what it will match after the change, using AND and OR explicitly, and confirm before updating.

The segment is processed asynchronously. Once it has finished processing, call get_segment with additional_fields_segment=['profile_count'] and tell the user the count, flagging it if it is much larger, or changed far more, than they expected.

